WEBVTT

00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:07.730
My good people, I am forever grateful that
you have assembled before me here this day.

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:13.490
Why, you may ask? Because you have chosen
to gracefully share in our peace and happiness!

00:00:13.490 --> 00:00:15.170
But let us not forget!

00:00:15.170 --> 00:00:18.080
This world is full of miscreants
who would seek to stop us!

00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:22.040
The hole is what once brought us the Yufang!

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.690
It brought us prosperity!

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:31.130
It brought airplanes, anti-air artillery, Yufang liquor,
curry and rice, and even pancakes!

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:37.760
But our enemies now wish to take
its blessings for themselves!

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:43.230
These heinous criminals spare
no thought for anyone but themselves!

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.080
These criminals are the people of Rahama!

00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:48.380
They tried to keep our long awaited new hole
all to themselves, but failed!

00:00:49.670 --> 00:00:52.110
And just like that it was gone once again.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:57.770
We of the Brotherhood of Freedom Union will not
forgive any who side with Rahama or Porokka!

00:00:57.990 --> 00:01:00.180
We must not allow these criminals to

00:01:00.180 --> 00:01:03.830
keep to themselves, stealing away 
the wonders of the holes from us!

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:07.460
The Brotherhood of Freedom Union
is the only path to world peace!

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:10.340
Because only the Brotherhood of Freedom Union
has the power to make it a reality!

00:01:10.340 --> 00:01:13.420
The Brotherhood of Freedom Union is the best!

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:16.960
That damn Isao!

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:17.930
How could he do this?

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:20.300
How could he set our beloved Porokka ablaze?!

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:24.130
Mr. Gaudreau, please settle down.
You'll only bring your blood pressure up.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:25.540
Blood pressure be damned!

00:01:25.540 --> 00:01:28.250
It's these Ikesuka bastards 
we need to worry about!

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:31.710
Mr. Gaudreau...

00:01:32.210 --> 00:01:34.290
Get in touch with Shouto!

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:36.710
And that haughty gal from Gadoll, too!

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:54.250
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:01:55.580 --> 00:01:58.720
Flying through the mesh of clouds

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:02.290
Our dancing wings wrap up in the wind

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:05.750
Stars fall right before our eyes

00:02:11.750 --> 00:02:15.040
The blue of all blues that drew us in

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.320
We kicked up off the blurring ground

00:02:18.320 --> 00:02:23.290
Let me hear the sound of the sky you know

00:02:25.870 --> 00:02:32.630
Take flight make gravity your ally

00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:39.040
One more time, however many 
times, laughing all along

00:02:39.040 --> 00:02:46.080
We would never look back when we fly

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:51.360
An everlasting dream we 
live in pursuit of tomorrow

00:02:51.360 --> 00:02:54.790
Amid rising despair I locked away my love

00:02:54.790 --> 00:02:57.080
I hate my weak self

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:03.040
Here and now passes by as 
we head towards the future

00:03:06.950 --> 00:03:12.830
Duel in Ikesuka

00:03:07.380 --> 00:03:10.420
He goes around preaching of brotherhood this and freedom that,

00:03:10.420 --> 00:03:12.610
but it's all just fancy talk.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:16.000
All he's after is consolidating
all power into his own hands!

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.130
How can they not see that?

00:03:17.130 --> 00:03:19.130
That's what we're here for, isn't it?

00:03:19.130 --> 00:03:20.380
You'd better believe it!

00:03:20.380 --> 00:03:22.850
Damned if I'll ever let 
Isao tell me what to do!

00:03:22.850 --> 00:03:25.460
If he did take control,
the world would be as good as finished.

00:03:25.460 --> 00:03:27.580
Ijitsu would be split into three classes.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:30.830
Isao, his followers, and...

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:32.960
His slaves.

00:03:35.290 --> 00:03:36.900
This is the Ofukouyama squad.

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.790
We've reached the target airspace.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:46.670
All right! We've got eyes on
the Union air force! On our ten!

00:03:46.670 --> 00:03:48.420
Looks like roughly a hundred fighters.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.080
That's fewer than intel reported.

00:03:50.080 --> 00:03:52.670
Another hundred or so, on our one o'clock.

00:03:52.670 --> 00:03:54.380
That puts them at around two hundred...

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.250
Okay everyone, are you ready for this?

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:57.040
You bet!

00:03:57.040 --> 00:04:00.590
You'll be safe with me 
covering you, captain Naomi!

00:04:00.590 --> 00:04:01.790
Yeah, no thanks.

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:05.260
What?! Come on! Don't be like that, captain!

00:04:05.260 --> 00:04:08.830
I'm Adolfo Yamada, of THE Nazarin--

00:04:08.830 --> 00:04:11.980
Camilla, you know what our job is
and what we're here to do, right?

00:04:11.980 --> 00:04:13.460
Don't you go chasing any of them down!

00:04:13.460 --> 00:04:15.210
Of course! A grudge is a grudge!

00:04:15.210 --> 00:04:18.440
Gotta stay calm, cool and collected!
Gotta riddle them with holes!

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:20.170
More importantly you gotta stay alive.

00:04:20.170 --> 00:04:20.930
Exactly.

00:04:20.930 --> 00:04:22.990
Now all fighters, prepare to engage!

00:04:22.990 --> 00:04:25.460
The Ofukouyama squad has 
moved to engage the enemy.

00:04:25.460 --> 00:04:28.170
Good! Good, good, good! 
They fell for it, then.

00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:32.290
Those idiots from Ikesuka and the Union
just threw two hundred fighters at a decoy!

00:04:32.290 --> 00:04:34.460
That's gotta be nearly all their aircraft.

00:04:34.460 --> 00:04:35.880
Don't let your guard down yet.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:38.040
They might still have more 
firepower than we know.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:40.920
C'mon now Julia, that doesn't sound like you.

00:04:40.920 --> 00:04:43.750
Overthinking things will 
just make you a coward!

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:46.630
We've got all the intel we need right here.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:48.180
Right, my faithful assistant, you?

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:52.960
Oh yes. According to my sources there
is no reason to doubt any of this.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:56.130
Well there you have it!

00:04:56.130 --> 00:04:59.460
We're gonna wipe 'em all 
out! Now let's move out!

00:04:59.460 --> 00:05:02.380
What is it with men like that who think shouting
their orders will make any difference?

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:05.360
I bet he thinks the louder he shouts
the more power he wields.

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:07.110
What an ingrate.

00:05:07.110 --> 00:05:09.710
Now now, girls. Let's curb 
the slander, shall we?

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:13.000
No, feel free. They're entirely 
right about Gaudreau there.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:17.210
But everything comes in 
handy when used properly.

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:19.580
And right know Porokka's military force
is just what we need.

00:05:19.580 --> 00:05:21.500
You seem pretty confident about all this.

00:05:21.500 --> 00:05:22.300
Of course.

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:26.460
We might be a rag tag assortment,
but we have them beat in sheer numbers.

00:05:26.460 --> 00:05:27.590
This is anyone's battle.

00:05:27.590 --> 00:05:31.430
I prefer to stay away from gambling
when I'm just as likely to lose as win.

00:05:31.430 --> 00:05:34.890
But if we pass up this opportunity,
our chances of winning only go down from here.

00:05:34.890 --> 00:05:37.250
So this is really our only chance, then.

00:05:37.250 --> 00:05:38.350
Exactly!

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:41.420
I sure hope Miki made it 
safely out of Porokka.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:45.000
I haven't heard word from 
her, and I'm so worried...

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:46.630
Why would she get in touch with you?

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:49.460
Why? I thought the madame sorted things out?

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:52.040
More like smoothed them over.
She never said she'd speak with you again.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:55.380
I'm sure you've guessed as much,
but we don't have any time to waste.

00:05:55.380 --> 00:05:57.870
First we need to hit the factories
producing those bombers!

00:05:57.870 --> 00:06:00.460
Right, and those would be where...?

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.170
Oh, yeah. Right there.

00:06:02.170 --> 00:06:05.880
Our target is 25 kilometers 
southwest of central Ikesuka.

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:07.630
The Fugaku construction assembly plant!

00:06:07.630 --> 00:06:09.390
Wind speeds are at 17 khrill, 
blowing in at 90 degrees.

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.290
First Officer, your orders, sir!

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:16.960
Move the bridge upwind! All 
engines, full speed ahead!

00:06:16.960 --> 00:06:18.000
On our twenty!

00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:20.920
Releasing the hatch! All 
fighters, prepare for takeoff!

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:28.330
Hey, so uhh, I don't really get what's going on here.
Isn't this kind of a cheap move?

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:29.760
Well we drew out their

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:32.950
main forces so we can close
in on their facilities, so you might say that.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.330
Diversions are perfectly 
acceptable military tactics.

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:40.210
I hate these missions, though.
It's such a pain when we can't just fly however we want!

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:46.210
I know what you mean, but I think we'd best avoid
being hasty and try and talk this all out.

00:06:46.210 --> 00:06:48.500
I would have to disagree.

00:06:48.500 --> 00:06:49.930
Oh my, and why's that?

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:53.850
Reona seems to be forgetting that there
are some people you just cannot reason with.

00:06:53.850 --> 00:06:57.680
The more trust you put in someone,
the weaker you are when facing them.

00:06:57.680 --> 00:07:00.310
That may be, but her word 
is still good by me.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.580
Right or wrong.

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:03.500
That's nonsensical.

00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:06.960
Where do you stand, Kate? 
Good or bad? Do it or don't?

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:08.330
There are things I wish to clear up.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:09.290
What's that supposed to mean?

00:07:09.290 --> 00:07:11.670
This mission is my chance to clear up
things I wish to make clear.

00:07:11.670 --> 00:07:12.830
What does that even mean?

00:07:31.420 --> 00:07:32.920
Kylie, quit lagging behind!

00:07:32.920 --> 00:07:34.140
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:34.140 --> 00:07:35.630
You're flying too low, too.

00:07:35.630 --> 00:07:36.880
Yeah, yeah.

00:07:36.880 --> 00:07:39.250
How can you be so lax?

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:41.830
Kylie has seemed out of 
it for a while now, huh?

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:43.750
Know what? I bet she's just scared!

00:07:43.750 --> 00:07:48.170
Nope. I was just thinking about what
we're actually supposed to be doing out here.

00:07:48.170 --> 00:07:49.500
At a time like this?

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:52.650
We're defending the Hagoromo 
and attacking Ikesuka.

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:56.330
Defending the Hagoromo I can understand,
but why are we attacking Ikesuka, again?

00:07:57.000 --> 00:08:00.680
Kylie! Were you in some other realm of existence
during our briefing or something?

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:05.310
No, I was listening.
But none of it really made sense to me.

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:08.790
So a hole almost opened over Rahama, right?

00:08:08.790 --> 00:08:10.420
Then Isao showed up?

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.500
And then Julia formed some kind of alliance.

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:14.800
I get all that.

00:08:15.920 --> 00:08:17.050
But then what?

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:19.750
What are we doing here?

00:08:20.960 --> 00:08:24.540
Are wars supposed to just be 
fought on a whim like this?

00:08:25.170 --> 00:08:28.290
Is that what the KOTOBUKI Corps stands for?

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:32.960
Orders are orders. And things 
are already in motion.

00:08:32.960 --> 00:08:34.950
The Magnificent
KOTOBUKI

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:04.060
I figured this lot was just a bunch of rag tag pilots,
but they're better than I thought!

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:06.270
Don't forget! This is for Shouto!

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:08.920
For the theater they leveled on First Avenue!

00:09:08.920 --> 00:09:13.960
For the bakery and the Takochu Park, too!
Let them have it!

00:09:28.540 --> 00:09:29.630
Got ya--

00:09:30.500 --> 00:09:33.960
My lady! I, the world's dandiest man,
am here by your side! Fear not!

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:36.050
Whaddya think you're doing, 
eggplant for brains?!

00:09:36.380 --> 00:09:40.170
When I'm maneuvering behind an enemy fighter you
should be making sure they can't pull away!

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:41.810
W-well how am I supposed to know that?

00:09:41.810 --> 00:09:45.750
If you have to ask, then quit talking yourself up!
You're just wasting your breath!

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:46.710
My lady, look out!

00:09:46.210 --> 00:09:47.920
Captain Naomi, on your five!

00:09:54.460 --> 00:09:55.660
What are you even out here for?

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:58.070
If you're just gonna float around 
up here, then quit wasting gasoline!

00:09:58.080 --> 00:09:59.460
I was trying to warn you...

00:09:59.460 --> 00:10:01.500
If you can't even cover me 
then you're good for nothing!

00:10:11.210 --> 00:10:13.580
Stay out of my line of sight, fish face!

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:14.670
Sorry...

00:10:31.270 --> 00:10:35.250
Pummel that factory,
and we'll really curb the Union's firepower!

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:43.750
Those big planes from the 
other day aren't here, huh?

00:10:43.750 --> 00:10:44.420
The Fugaku?

00:10:44.420 --> 00:10:45.290
Yeah, those!

00:10:45.290 --> 00:10:47.660
Perhaps the bombers we saw
the other day were their whole fleet?

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:49.880
That still doesn't explain why this place seems
deserted.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:54.180
You'd figure they'd leave behind at least enough
people to defend the place.

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:55.210
We're blowing this place up?

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:58.080
Don't sweat the details. Light the place up!

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:00.040
Where's our welcoming committee?

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:04.170
There's no sight of 'em here.
I bet they all ran away scared of us!

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:05.930
Madame! Councilor Julia!

00:11:19.040 --> 00:11:19.670
It was a trap?!

00:11:19.670 --> 00:11:21.040
I count 200- No, wait...

00:11:21.040 --> 00:11:24.580
That's impossible!
They don't have those sort of numbers!

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:27.240
What happened to that 
perfect intel of yours?!

00:11:27.240 --> 00:11:30.790
Gaudreau, sir, it would seem despite
all unlikelihood that you were wrong.

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:31.710
I was what, now?!

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:33.920
I believe it is about time 
I make a career change.

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:35.080
RESIGNATION

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.420
The pleasure has been all mine!

00:11:36.540 --> 00:11:38.960
Are you telling me you were a double agent?!

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:42.040
You have my best wishes!

00:12:07.630 --> 00:12:08.540
Send the order to retreat.

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:10.480
If we don't do so this instant,

00:12:10.480 --> 00:12:12.930
our fifty-fifty chance
will quickly become much more of a gamble.

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:13.630
We can't!

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:17.040
Julia, it would seem we made light of Isao.

00:12:17.710 --> 00:12:18.550
We've lost.

00:12:21.420 --> 00:12:22.460
Full retreat!

00:12:22.460 --> 00:12:23.760
Turn us around!

00:12:23.760 --> 00:12:25.000
Turning now!

00:12:25.000 --> 00:12:26.270
Bearing 180!

00:12:26.270 --> 00:12:27.750
Alert the decoy squad!

00:12:27.750 --> 00:12:28.630
Roger!

00:12:28.630 --> 00:12:33.040
Gaudreau, it's Julia.
The Hagoromo is retreating. You'd best as well.

00:12:33.040 --> 00:12:37.170
Retreat isn't even on the table for us!

00:12:37.170 --> 00:12:38.580
You'll be wiped out at this rate!

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:40.920
It's talk like that that's 
gonna cost us this battle!

00:12:40.920 --> 00:12:42.460
We can still win!

00:12:42.460 --> 00:12:45.170
And so the tricksters 
have become the tricked.

00:12:45.170 --> 00:12:47.420
Do you have any other 
options or back up plans?

00:12:47.420 --> 00:12:49.040
Not really, no!

00:12:49.040 --> 00:12:50.710
But this is just too cruel...

00:12:50.710 --> 00:12:55.250
Why don't you call that ex-wife of yours?
She might even worry about you, now.

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:56.710
Even now, it's only a "might"?

00:12:57.040 --> 00:13:00.000
Come on! Go away!

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:00.960
Whew!

00:13:01.500 --> 00:13:03.010
Thank you, Naomi!

00:13:03.010 --> 00:13:05.590
How do they expect us to 
retreat from all this?!

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:11.210
Well, we can't just have you running off
without paying for what you've done.

00:13:11.210 --> 00:13:13.390
This time it's our turn!

00:13:13.390 --> 00:13:16.710
I would appreciate it if you would
stick around with us just a tad longer.

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:21.960
Hmph, fine then.

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:24.290
Those Type 5's aren't half bad, huh?

00:13:26.880 --> 00:13:28.750
I sure love these near death battles!

00:13:28.750 --> 00:13:31.000
You two bastards better keep up!

00:13:31.000 --> 00:13:31.630
What?!

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:32.490
Aren't we retreating?

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:33.630
That one there's all yours!

00:13:33.630 --> 00:13:35.710
All my- What?!

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:48.300
Engines 21 and 23 have been knocked out!

00:13:50.080 --> 00:13:51.850
Engine 12 has been knocked clean off!

00:13:51.850 --> 00:13:54.060
We can't go at 'em like this!

00:13:52.130 --> 00:13:54.080
Fires have broken out in hangars 1 and 2!

00:13:54.060 --> 00:13:55.130
You have to retreat!

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:58.540
So much for your day of dominance, huh?!

00:13:58.540 --> 00:13:59.960
I never claimed such to begin with!

00:14:04.250 --> 00:14:07.880
Dammit! How am I supposed to face up to Chika
if I can't even put her teachings to work here?!

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:09.210
Keep your wits about you, Tokiwagi!

00:14:09.210 --> 00:14:11.330
Don't take this too far!
We need to focus on each of them, one by one!

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:12.330
You ain't gotta tell me!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.750
Rahama still has its secret weapon!

00:14:16.750 --> 00:14:18.930
And it's time you had a taste of it!

00:14:18.930 --> 00:14:21.880
Fires have broken out in block 13!
We can't put these out!

00:14:21.880 --> 00:14:24.760
Keep at it! The enemy's falling back!

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:26.720
All we gotta do is push 
through this, and we win!

00:14:35.500 --> 00:14:37.080
Are you seeing this? 
Something just went down!

00:14:37.080 --> 00:14:38.100
The Hagoromo?!

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.500
It appears to be the Porokka flagship.

00:14:39.500 --> 00:14:40.500
How could this be?

00:14:40.500 --> 00:14:41.490
Reona...

00:14:41.490 --> 00:14:42.500
We retreat!

00:14:42.500 --> 00:14:43.790
Fall back and protect the Hagoromo!

00:14:43.790 --> 00:14:44.580
Got it!

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:53.000
What the heck is that thing?!

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:55.660
Oh yeah! This is what I call a scuffle!

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:58.790
May the last plane flying win!

00:14:58.790 --> 00:15:00.170
Oh, this is so exciting!

00:15:09.420 --> 00:15:11.330
Isao, sir, please fall back.

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:13.970
There is no need for you to fly 
head-first into this conflict.

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:17.210
How did that saying go again? 
That old Yufang one...

00:15:17.210 --> 00:15:17.920
What?

00:15:17.920 --> 00:15:18.580
Oh yeah!

00:15:18.580 --> 00:15:21.000
The real fool's the fool that 
doesn't fool around at all!

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:44.840
Zara, will you fly with me?

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:47.050
I'm with you.

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:53.930
I assume that's you,
Brotherhood of Freedom Union Chairman, Isao!

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:54.670
Huh?

00:15:54.670 --> 00:15:58.890
I'm Reona, captain of the Ouni Company's
KOTOBUKI Corps from Rahama!

00:15:59.130 --> 00:16:03.250
When I was still a fresh pilot, 
you once saved my life.

00:16:03.580 --> 00:16:05.130
I just want to talk with you!

00:16:05.860 --> 00:16:09.830
Uhh, talk about what, exactly?
I don't like talking about complicated stuff!

00:16:10.250 --> 00:16:11.670
I don't want to have to 
fight any pointless battles.

00:16:12.000 --> 00:16:14.420
I'm sure neither of us wish to see
the loss of any more lives!

00:16:14.920 --> 00:16:16.000
That's true.

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:19.210
If you issue the order,
our side will surely agree to a ceasefire.

00:16:19.540 --> 00:16:21.000
I'll do what I can to make sure of it!

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:22.670
Yes, yes, and then?

00:16:22.670 --> 00:16:24.250
Please allow us to retreat!

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:33.760
Sure.

00:16:34.710 --> 00:16:38.080
I knew you were not the person 
everyone says you are!

00:16:43.830 --> 00:16:44.770
Just kidding!

00:16:44.770 --> 00:16:45.630
Reona!

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:54.330
I told you I don't like getting
all caught up in complicated stuff!

00:16:57.450 --> 00:16:58.750
How dare you do that to her!

00:17:09.630 --> 00:17:11.850
Well, lookie here, another new face!

00:17:11.850 --> 00:17:13.420
Hi there, newbie!

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:15.170
I'm no newbie, I'm Kylie!

00:17:15.170 --> 00:17:16.640
We met in Areshima!

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:18.170
And back with that fish, too!

00:17:18.170 --> 00:17:19.290
We did?

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:22.830
You know, I think I do remember
that mark on your tail, there.

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:26.080
But I don't remember you being 
a girl. Or young, either!

00:17:26.080 --> 00:17:26.600
What?!

00:17:26.960 --> 00:17:31.360
It was just some old fool who got left behind
when the Yufang disappeared from Ijitsu.

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:33.000
A real stubborn guy.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:36.120
Indeed. A mulish man stuck in his old ways.

00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:42.750
We call them them the Yufang here, but they call
themselves the Japanese Army, you know!

00:17:42.750 --> 00:17:44.700
Yes, indeed. Not the 
Yufang, but the Japanese.

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:47.960
Apparently that guy was some
sorta "mill-ee-terry" engineer or something.

00:17:47.960 --> 00:17:51.670
But no matter how many times we talked,
he'd never listen to what we told him.

00:17:49.960 --> 00:17:51.670
ALTITUDE

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.500
OIL PRESSURE
FUEL PRESSURE

00:17:51.670 --> 00:17:53.510
He even tried fleeing.

00:17:54.380 --> 00:17:55.420
Ol' Sab...!

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:57.330
Maybe he just didn't like to fight?

00:17:57.880 --> 00:17:59.290
Despised it, I'm sure.

00:17:59.510 --> 00:18:00.990
Who knows, though?

00:18:00.990 --> 00:18:04.000
Indeed, we have no way of knowing now.

00:18:04.000 --> 00:18:05.100
Nope!

00:18:06.210 --> 00:18:08.040
'Cause he was such a pain 
that we shot him down!

00:18:09.420 --> 00:18:10.800
Stinks to be him, huh?

00:18:10.800 --> 00:18:14.900
Abandoned by the Yufang only to be shot down by me.
Not a happy ending!

00:18:14.900 --> 00:18:16.540
I wonder what he's up to now?

00:18:16.920 --> 00:18:19.420
Probably rotting away somewhere 
out in the wastelands.

00:18:20.960 --> 00:18:23.960
You miserable stinkin' buttface!

00:18:24.670 --> 00:18:26.420
Lemme tell you about Ol' Sab!

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:28.320
Huh? What? What's the matter?

00:18:28.320 --> 00:18:29.630
Ol' Sab!

00:18:30.580 --> 00:18:34.050
He hated people like you!

00:18:40.220 --> 00:18:42.040
We can shoot down one after another,
but there's no end!

00:18:42.040 --> 00:18:43.380
Chika, on your two o'clock!

00:18:43.380 --> 00:18:44.040
Above you!

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:56.040
They've just got far 
stronger engines onboard!

00:18:56.040 --> 00:18:57.250
What are we gonna do?

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:04.700
Chika, here they come! Get ready to evade!

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:05.500
Gotcha!

00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:21.290
We got them!

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.920
Chika! That was excellent!

00:19:34.920 --> 00:19:37.040
Yikes! People can see my 
underwear from down there!

00:19:37.040 --> 00:19:40.710
I'll be right down to pick 
you up. You just sit tight.

00:19:43.080 --> 00:19:45.450
Engines 2, 4, and 6 are down!

00:19:45.450 --> 00:19:48.580
Engines 1 and 7 at 30% output!

00:19:47.040 --> 00:19:49.830
This is bad. Real bad!

00:19:49.830 --> 00:19:52.170
Then why do you look so excited?

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:54.930
I was just thinking how I feel so alive!

00:19:54.930 --> 00:19:58.050
I suppose you won't really 
"feel" it when we're dead.

00:19:55.460 --> 00:19:58.050
Helium leaks in sections 
2 and 4 cannot be stopped!

00:19:58.050 --> 00:20:01.100
We'll need to abandon the 
ballast on the bow to realign!

00:20:01.100 --> 00:20:04.040
They really won't make this 
easy for us, will they?

00:20:04.040 --> 00:20:04.790
Mayor!

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:05.890
Coming, coming!

00:20:05.890 --> 00:20:07.380
Enemy formation coming in on our nine!

00:20:07.380 --> 00:20:11.100
All right, all right!
I can't handle them all with this thing, you know!

00:20:19.830 --> 00:20:22.210
I'm done for!

00:20:23.500 --> 00:20:28.450
Mind if we join you, then?
In this big gamble, I mean big opportunity here?!

00:20:28.450 --> 00:20:29.040
Who's that?

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:29.580
Who is that?

00:20:29.580 --> 00:20:30.290
Who are you?

00:20:30.290 --> 00:20:34.170
The CEO and big boss of 
Elite Industries, Torihei!

00:20:34.170 --> 00:20:35.290
Here they come!

00:20:43.920 --> 00:20:44.890
Seriously though, what?

00:20:52.100 --> 00:20:56.040
Aw, here I was thinking maybe he'd taught you
a thing or two, but I guess not, huh?

00:20:56.040 --> 00:20:58.980
That old man wasn't good for much,
but he was great in the cockpit

00:20:58.980 --> 00:21:01.190
of his Zero there, at least.

00:21:01.190 --> 00:21:02.130
He flew it like a hawk!

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.170
Buh-bye, now.

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:22.460
Will we meet again?

00:21:23.630 --> 00:21:24.970
Nope, I doubt it!

00:21:28.720 --> 00:21:29.850
Carelessness is your worst enemy.

00:21:30.420 --> 00:21:32.750
Thanks, I'll keep that in mind...

00:21:32.750 --> 00:21:34.080
There's something I want to ask you.

00:21:34.460 --> 00:21:36.420
Are you the one who shot Allen down?

00:21:36.420 --> 00:21:37.290
I sure am.

00:21:46.420 --> 00:21:50.500
I wanted to try and soar through that sky

00:21:50.500 --> 00:21:54.330
So I wished upon the winds right before me

00:21:54.330 --> 00:21:58.290
Our aspirations build us scenery

00:21:58.290 --> 00:22:02.710
I wonder how that wind is now

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:11.040
Why do we fight, I wonder

00:22:11.040 --> 00:22:15.080
What is our purpose here?

00:22:15.080 --> 00:22:23.290
I asked, but the skies do not answer

00:22:24.000 --> 00:22:30.960
We all have wings

00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:35.710
Far away at the end of all lament

00:22:35.710 --> 00:22:39.960
The stories we found

00:22:39.960 --> 00:22:47.680
No one can steal these skies away

00:22:47.680 --> 00:22:52.420
We will soar unafraid of anything

00:22:52.420 --> 00:22:59.540
Because happiness is right here

00:23:12.830 --> 00:23:13.920
Come on, over here!

00:23:13.920 --> 00:23:15.000
Move, move, move!

00:23:16.540 --> 00:23:17.500
What's the situation?

00:23:17.500 --> 00:23:19.000
Do you even need to ask?!

00:23:19.000 --> 00:23:20.210
It's a load of garbage!

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:21.250
Understood.

00:23:21.250 --> 00:23:23.590
Kate is returning with Kylie aboard.

00:23:24.580 --> 00:23:27.190
Well I hope you're all in the 
mood for a grand surprise!

00:23:27.190 --> 00:23:28.340
Another hole's about to open

00:23:29.130 --> 00:23:29.960
Where?

00:23:30.670 --> 00:23:31.550
Right here!

00:23:31.550 --> 00:23:33.670
Right above Ikesuka.

00:23:34.250 --> 00:23:35.540
And you wait until now to tell us?!

00:23:35.890 --> 00:23:37.900
Preview

00:23:36.130 --> 00:23:40.580
Next time on The Magnificent KOTOBUKI,
"KOTOBUKI of the Setting Sun"!

00:23:37.900 --> 00:23:40.880
KOTOBUKI of the Setting Sun
